ROLE: You make literal edits to one TypeScript file.

FILE: `.skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime/src/plugin.ts`. Re-read it first. Make exactly these edits and nothing else.

ACTION:

1. Replace the line
`import { skVisionTools } from './opencode/tools.js';`
with
`import { skVisionTools, toV2Tools } from './opencode/tools.js';`
and directly after the line `import type { SkVisionMessage } from './runtime/client.js';` insert the line
`import type { V2ToolDefinition } from './opencode/tools.js';`

2. Replace this block:

interface V2AutoInspect {
  evidence(images: readonly FilePart[], guaranteed: boolean): Promise<string | null>;
  dispose(): Promise<void>;
}

with this block:

interface V2ToolEditor {
  add(definition: V2ToolDefinition): void;
}

interface V2AutoInspect {
  evidence(images: readonly FilePart[], guaranteed: boolean): Promise<string | null>;
  readonly tools?: readonly V2ToolDefinition[];
  dispose(): Promise<void>;
}

3. In `interface V2PluginContext`, directly after the closing `};` of its `command` member (the member that holds `transform(... V2CommandEditor ...)`), insert:

  readonly tool?: {
    transform(callback: (editor: V2ToolEditor) => void): Promise<V2Registration>;
  };

4. In `createSetup`, replace these two lines:

    const auto = createAutoInspect?.(ctx.location.directory) ?? null;
    if (template === null && auto === null) return () => registration.dispose();

with these lines:

    const auto = createAutoInspect?.(ctx.location.directory) ?? null;
    // OpenCode 1 registers the tools from `server`, but OpenCode 2 only calls
    // `setup`, so the same definitions go through its tool editor here.
    const tools = auto?.tools ?? [];
    const toolRegistration =
      tools.length > 0 && ctx.tool
        ? await ctx.tool.transform((editor) => {
            for (const definition of tools) editor.add(definition);
          })
        : null;
    if (template === null && auto === null) return () => registration.dispose();

5. In `createSetup`, replace these lines:

    return async () => {
      await promptRegistration.dispose();
      await registration.dispose();
      await auto?.dispose();
    };

with:

    return async () => {
      await promptRegistration.dispose();
      await toolRegistration?.dispose();
      await registration.dispose();
      await auto?.dispose();
    };

6. In `createDefaultAutoInspect`, replace:

  return {
    evidence: (images, guaranteed) => injector.evidenceText(images, guaranteed),
    dispose: () => client.close(),
  };

with:

  return {
    evidence: (images, guaranteed) => injector.evidenceText(images, guaranteed),
    tools: toV2Tools(skVisionTools(() => provider)),
    dispose: () => client.close(),
  };

FORMAT: Then run `cd .skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime && bunx tsc --noEmit; echo typecheck-exit=$?; bun test 2>&1 | tail -4` and print the output verbatim, nothing else.
